# What this package may never name, anywhere under lib/ and test/.
#
# THE TEST FOR A WORD: could a vendor with the same tool and a completely different product still
# use this package with that word in it? A name the tool gives itself passes and stays off this
# list — kube-system, cert-manager and default-ipv4-ippool are names kubernetes, cert-manager and
# calico give themselves. A name of one product built on a cluster fails and goes on it.
#
# One word per line. Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored; everything else is matched
# case-insensitively and word-anchored, so a longer name that merely contains a word is no
# occurrence of it.
#
# WORD-ANCHORED CUTS BOTH WAYS, and the blocks below are written knowing it. Anything that is not a
# letter or a digit ends a word, so a bare name reports every longer one built on it with a
# separator, and a longer name built WITHOUT a separator is a different word that has to stand in
# its own right — `digita` does not report `digitacloud`.
#
# THE LIST LIVES HERE, UNDER tool/, AND NOT BESIDE THE CHECK THAT READS IT. The scan reads test/ to
# the byte, so a list written into test/checks/tool_purity_test.dart would itself be an occurrence
# of every word on it and the check could never pass. That tool/ stays out of the scan is asserted
# by a counter-probe of its own.

# The product this package was cut out of, the platform it stands on, and the organisation behind
# both. This block stands on every list in this tree, word for word.
hostyour
digita
digitacloud
digitaplatform
simetrix
simetrixch

# That product's choices: the distribution it runs on, the components it deploys, the tools it
# drives those components with, the vendors it rents from, and the name it gave its certificate
# issuer. Each is a fact of one product, not of kubectl the tool or the cluster it drives. This
# block stands on every list in this tree, except that a package never carries its OWN tool —
# kubectl is this package's, which is why that word is the one of this kind missing here.
#
# THE ONE WORD THIS LIST IS NARROWER ON THAN EVERY OTHER, AND WHY. Every other list in this tree
# carries the bare word `letsencrypt`, which reports the longer name below and every SCREAMING_SNAKE
# name built on it as well. Here it would also report
# lib/src/steps/write_cluster_issuer_manifest.dart:98, where the name a program answers the operator's
# mailbox under still carries one authority's name. That name is not this package's to change alone:
# it is read out of the answer file and out of the program rows that declare it, both of which live
# outside this repository, so renaming it here alone would leave every run refused for a missing
# answer. Until that name is changed on both sides, this list stays on the longer word and the gap
# is written down rather than hidden.
microk8s
argocd
tekton
zot
authentik
external-secrets
vault
helm
snap
netplan
cloudflare
hetzner
letsencrypt-prod

# That product's own domain words, and its own word for the branch every other branch is cut from.
# Git has no "trunk" — it has a branch, and a start point a new branch is cut from — so a comment or
# a fixture that said trunk would be carrying one product's name for a branch into every cluster
# this package ever met.
tenant
consumer
trunk
